      "title": "addr_resolv: Don't continually look up ethers that didn't resolve",
      "message": "addr_resolv: Don't continually look up ethers that didn't resolve\n\nIf there's a EUI-48 that we tried to resolve but it didn't resolve\nat all, presumably because it's locally administered and we didn't\neven find a OUI/MA-M/MA-S in the manuf file, don't keep trying to\nresolve it on future accesses. In particular, this tries to open\nboth ethers files (which may not exist.)\n\nIt's good enough to reset checking the ethers file upon loading\na new file (note that the old behavior didn't change the lookup\nif an entry in the ethers file changes or disappeared, only if it\nwasn't there and was added.)\n\nFix the worst case of #19915. We probably still want to load the\nethers file(s) once when opening a file, or at the very least cache\ntheir non-existence. We also might want to separate \"resolve MAC\naddresses to OUI/MA-M/MA-S\" from \"resolve MAC addresses to hostnames\"\n(#11470), though that begs the question of how to deal with certain\nWell Known Addresses that specify all 6 bytes of the EUI-48. It\nalso might change the relative precedence of resolution (#18075)\nwithout being careful.\n",
